ble poll is 48 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Cindy Hyde-Smith (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith seeks reelection in a state that leaned Republican by eleven points at the presidential level, giving the incumbent a strong structural advantage. Most nonpartisan raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Hyde-Smith roughly a ninety percent chance of winning.\n\nStill, there are signs of life for Democrats. Recent polls sponsored by Democratic groups show the gap in the mid-single digits, well inside the state's partisan lean, and challenger Scott Colom has raised a competitive sum while drawing outside support and national attention, including campaign visits from Senator Cory Booker. The forecast keeps Hyde-Smith a clear but not absolute favorite, with an expected margin near eleven points and meaningful uncertainty given thin and dated polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0354, "margin": -10.93}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0452, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0338, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0557, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0878, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0513, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.051, "margin": -11.0}]}